@startuml malicious_verifier_attack
title Malicious verifier attack

database "Blockchain\n(BC) " as BC
actor "Adversary\n(A)" as A
participant "Smart Contract\n(SC)" as SC
actor "Campaign Initiator\n(B)" as B
database "IPFS" as IPFS
actor "Honest Sender\n(S)" as S


== Sender submits data ==

S -> IPFS : Upload Enc(data, K_enc)
S -> SC : Submit CID_ciphered

note over A : A can join at any time\nand retrieve all the data
== Verifier enrollment ==

A -> SC : Enroll as Verifier
B -> SC : Deliver K_dec to A
SC -> A : K_dec

note over A : A now holds K_dec\nafter this moment A\ndoesn't need to interact with SC

== A exploits public blockchain visibility ==

A -> BC : Read CID_ciphered
A -> A : CID = Dec(CID_ciphered, K_dec)
A -> IPFS : Retrieve encrypted data using CID
IPFS --> A : Enc(data, K_enc)
A -> A : data = Dec(Enc(data, K_enc), K_dec)

note over A #FAECE7
  A can decrypt data from any sender
  without being elected to the
  corresponding verification slot
end note

@enduml